  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Road Safety Phase 2 Multi Donor Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The Global Road Safety Facility has established itself as a global funding mechanism for the delivery of road safety solutions to low and middle income client countries.
 
 The UN declaration for a Decade of Action for Road Safety was endorsed by large number of the Bank&apos;s client countries, there is an urgency to deliver solutions that will meet the Decade goals of stabilizing and reducing global deaths and injuries due to traffic crashes, by 2020.
 
 The objective of the Trust Fund is to build on past achievements and continue to develop capacity to support the sustainable reduction in road deaths and injuries.
 
 This intiative is well aligned to the Bank&apos;s Post Crisis Directions Strategy. Over 90% of deaths and injuries occurs in the LMICs and is estimated to cost between 1 and 3% of GDP.  Deaths from crashes are the second highest killer of children between 5 and 15 in Africa.  Creating strong institutional frameworks for adressing road safety,improves the condition for the most poor and vulnerable and strengthens governance.  It is also a key pivot of Banks Transport Strategy &apos;Safe, Clean and Affordable Transport&apos;
 
 Through development of knowledge tools for infrastructure and capacity assessments, improved governance and data collection, the Facility has a solid platform from which to work with client countries and organizations to provide appropriate and sustainable solutions to the road safety crisis.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
